From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: v8: ppc64 move the TruncateDoubleToI stub call out of line

kArchTruncateDoubleToI calls MacroAssembler::TruncateDoubleToI, which lays
the whole conversion in the hot stream:

    fctidz f13,fN
    mffprd rT,f13
    extsw  rS,rT
    cmpd   rS,rT
    beq    done           in range: jump over the stub call
    mflr   rS             -- slow path, 11 instructions, inline --
    stdu   rS,-8(sp)
    stfdu  fN,-8(sp)
    ld     ip,<DoubleToI>(kRootRegister)
    mtctr  ip
    bctrl
    ld     rT,0(sp)
    addi   sp,sp,8
    ld     rS,0(sp)
    addi   sp,sp,8
    mtlr   rS
  done:

Every in-range truncation -- ToInt32 of a double that already is an int32,
i.e. nearly all of them -- takes a forward branch over eleven instructions
of stub call that sit in the instruction stream and the fetch window.  x64
keeps four instructions inline (cvttsd2siq, cmpq, jo, movl) and emits the
call in OutOfLineTruncateDoubleToI.  Do the same here with this file's
OutOfLineCode mechanism:

    fctidz f13,fN
    mffprd rT,f13
    extsw  rS,rT
    cmpd   rS,rT
    bne    ool            out of range: go to the stub
  exit:

and the eleven instructions above, then the jump back to exit, in the
out-of-line block at the end of the function with the other slow paths.
Five instructions inline against sixteen, no taken branch on the fast path,
and the slow path's contents are unchanged.

The fast path is built from the macro-assembler's own pieces,
ConvertDoubleToInt64 and TestIfInt32, rather than TryInlineTruncateDoubleToI,
because that helper branches to its done label on success and falls through
into the stub call, the wrong polarity for an out-of-line target.  The
out-of-line block is a copy of MacroAssembler::TruncateDoubleToI's slow
path with the same StubCallMode handling for wasm, so TruncateDoubleToI and
its other callers are untouched: the macro-assembler keeps emitting inline
for them, which is the limit of what this file alone can change.

Branch distance: the bne to the out-of-line entry is a 16-bit bc
displacement, the same form this file already uses for every other
out-of-line entry (write barriers, traps) and for deoptimisation exits.

The slow path still saves and restores LR itself, as it does today, so
frame-elided code needs nothing extra, and the sp adjustments stay balanced
inside the block.  No benchmark was run for this change; the justification
is the instruction count above and that ToInt32 is on the path of every
bitwise operator and typed-array index applied to a double.

Valid for both pools: nothing ISA-level changes; fctidz, mffprd (ISA 2.07),
extsw and cmpd are what the file already emits.  Independent of the other
two patches in this set; applies on top of them or on the unpatched file.

--- a/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/code-generator-ppc.cc
+++ b/v8/src/compiler/backend/ppc/code-generator-ppc.cc
@@ -281,6 +281,53 @@
   Zone* zone_;
 };
 
+class OutOfLineTruncateDoubleToI final : public OutOfLineCode {
+ public:
+  OutOfLineTruncateDoubleToI(CodeGenerator* gen, Register result,
+                             DoubleRegister input, StubCallMode stub_mode)
+      : OutOfLineCode(gen),
+        result_(result),
+        input_(input)
+#if V8_ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY
+        ,
+        stub_mode_(stub_mode)
+#endif  // V8_ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY
+  {
+  }
+
+  void Generate() final {
+    // The slow path of MacroAssembler::TruncateDoubleToI, unchanged: call
+    // the DoubleToI builtin with the input in a stack slot and read the
+    // result back from the same slot.
+    __ PushLR();
+    __ stfdu(input_, MemOperand(sp, -kDoubleSize));
+#if V8_ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY
+    if (stub_mode_ == StubCallMode::kCallWasmRuntimeStub) {
+      // A direct call to a wasm runtime stub defined in this module.  Just
+      // encode the stub index; it is patched when the code is added to the
+      // native module and copied into wasm code space.
+      __ Call(static_cast<Address>(Builtin::kDoubleToI),
+              RelocInfo::WASM_STUB_CALL);
+#else
+    // For balance.
+    if (false) {
+#endif  // V8_ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY
+    } else {
+      __ CallBuiltin(Builtin::kDoubleToI);
+    }
+    __ LoadU64(result_, MemOperand(sp));
+    __ addi(sp, sp, Operand(kDoubleSize));
+    __ PopLR();
+  }
+
+ private:
+  Register const result_;
+  DoubleRegister const input_;
+#if V8_ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY
+  StubCallMode const stub_mode_;
+#endif  // V8_ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY
+};
+
 #if V8_ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY
 class OutOfLineTrap final : public OutOfLineCode {
  public:
@@ -1204,12 +1251,22 @@
